tion policy consumes or verifies actual violations from the cited runtime producer."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Operational claims must cite implementation or observations that others can inspect."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "M-recommendation-bindings runtime cross-reference.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "invariant.clj and invariant_runner.clj are identified as the runtime that emits violations."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined evidence pattern and runtime source references.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A recommendation grounded in inspectable runtime violation evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [8], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion"} {:pattern-rationale "A proof-debt count should remain connected to the script and boundary inputs that determine it.", :fragment-span {:start 1031, :end 1137}, :occurrence-id ["measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number" 10], :roles ["dependency" "action"], :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :sentence-id "s13", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Pattern warrant requirement applied to the proof-debt measurement.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whether proof-debt-sensitive recommendations retain the counter rule, boundary inputs, and relevant exclusions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A computed metric must carry its rule, inputs, and assumptions so a skeptical reader can recompute it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "M-recommendation-bindings proof-debt counter fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "devmap_readiness.py and boundary.edn produce an active per-prototype proof-debt count."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined measurement pattern and proof-debt counter reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A next-move recommendation whose proof-debt value is reproducible from its cited computation and data."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [10], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number"} {:pattern-rationale "The empirical posterior remains interpretable only when its prior and live-evidence inputs accompany the resulting value.", :fragment-span {:start 1138, :end 1271}, :occurrence-id ["measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number" 11], :roles ["dependency" "rationale" "action"], :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :sentence-id "s14", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Pattern warrant discipline applied to the cited posterior construction.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whether its posterior-based policy preserves the prior, live evidence, join rule, and assumptions used to rank the complete set of moves."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number IF/THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A decision metric remains contestable and reproducible only when its generating warrant accompanies it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "M-recommendation-bindings AIF join fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "aif_join.cljs provides a precedent for combining a cached prior and live evidence into an empirical posterior."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined measurement pattern and aif_join.cljs precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "An empirical next-move posterior that can be recomputed and challenged at the join step."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [11], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number"} {:pattern-rationale "Binding the recommendation to an operational target makes the downstream next move observable and therefore checkable.", :fragment-span {:start 1272, :end 1402}, :occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 12], :roles ["dependency" "goal"], :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :sentence-id "s15", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Pattern evidence requirement applied to the downstream observation dependency.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whethe