ing paragraph; the L18 v3 complete search receipt runs/L18-remainder.edn.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Shared problem node and learning-loop dependency.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The sibling should inherit established mining discipline."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Work happens in or consumes the data-mining section's patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Corpus mining shares documented lessons and evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The section's own documentation states the problem: \"Lessons distilled from the futon6 meme-mining (forward: turns -> memes/methods) and goals-and-holes (backward: turns -> C-entries/belly) runs on a rented GPU box, 2026-06-25/26. They generalize to any pipeline that runs a model over a large corpus to extract structured records\" (source: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md reference to M-learning-loop.md.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-learning-loop is the pattern-learning sibling."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    This node is the landing point for @why edges from the data-mining worklist members (mechanical pass, row L18 v3); per-pattern questions route to the section documentation, not to invention here.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Mission cross-reference under the corpus-mining pattern.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Route mining questions through M-learning-loop and its documentation."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons" 15], :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons\" 15]", :span {:start 1007, :end 1070}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0", :square-digest "fc6d0184c8171f5cf5c358f892f3466b4a7016c58fc7ff744ba9622ea0bb09e1"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons", :objects {:G {:text "    A section whose documentation states one shared problem carries one problem node, not per-pattern copies (the L11/L15/L18 cost finding).\n\n    + evidence: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph; the L18 v3 complete search receipt runs/L18-remainder.edn.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Single-problem-node rule and shared substrate.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "A shared representation permits a geometry projection without a duplicate method."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Work happens in or consumes the data-mining section's patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg HOWEVER/THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Large-corpus extraction should reuse shared mining evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The section's own documentation states the problem: \"Lessons distilled from the futon6 meme-mining (forward: turns -> memes/methods) and goals-and-holes (backward: turns -> C-entries/belly) runs on a rented GPU box, 2026-06-25/26. They generalize to any pipeline that runs a model over a large corpus to extract structured records\" (source: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md shared-substrate fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The learning loop shares embeddings and rendering with geometry."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    This node is the landing point for @why edges from the data-mining worklist members (mechanical pass, row L18 v3); per-pattern questions route to the section documentation, not to invention here.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Mission fragment and corpus-mining documentation rule.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Expose geometry as a typed projection in the existing mining pipeline."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph" 17], :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :roles ["dependency" "goal"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph\" 17]", :span {:start 1155, :end 1201}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :square-digest "bbe567e82deeda4d3d1c5e35dee7f70140c375b83ff79c9f4f7c0b697cd84e7a"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Hypergraph-world model and operator dependency.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Click/Tick analysis acts on the geometry’s real hypergraph."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The Futon stack is the mutable shared hypergraph world."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md operator cross-reference.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-hypergraph-operator is the future Click/Tick consumer."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Mission dependency interpreted through world-is-hypergraph.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Make the real stack legible for the later operator layer."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph" 18], :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph\" 18]", :span {:start 1206, :end 1239}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :square-digest "f3765226578bfea7bfdeba1409823ec077fd8c273abf528fc40f84d57cd75285"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern topology and explicit layer ordering.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Geometry exposes structure; the operator analyzes it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Typed nodes and hyperedges form a navigable real world."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md layer-position fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The analytic layer sits above Stack Geometry."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Mission ordering mapped to the hypergraph pattern.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Keep topology in geometry and behavior in the operator layer."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 19], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 19]", :span {:start 1270, :end 1305}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "ecae1c0791493e96111385b293e7db7374229618047c760b3d364b482f985386"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "HDM rule and cited excursion.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "A recorded bridge can govern mission-record activation."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Activation ingests durable sources while retaining origin links."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md reference to E-webarxana-as-hinge-log-backend.md.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The WebArxana hinge-log excursion records an ingestion precedent."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Cross-reference interpreted through HDM.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Reuse the excursion’s bridge for Stack Geometry entities."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 20], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["dependency" "rationale"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 20]", :span {:start 1316, :end 1371}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "3fd38413a0d5651873ec457aee99fc421ff0cf8a627167f12f916f2c915db0eb"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "HDM mapping rule and Shape A precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "A bridge makes the storage-to-graph transition explicit."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Graph activation preserves mappings back to origins."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md Shape A fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Shape A is the precedent for landing mission entities."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Mission precedent mapped to HDM activation.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Apply Shape A while preserving entity source identity."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 21], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["dependency" "action"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 21]", :span {:start 1379, :end 1417}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "943d58b42d87c98e4209e6d588b15d2e096a2a19c92839fb0745c89f4b973a34"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "HDM purpose and named route.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Storage and rendering are stages of one activation path."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Stored entities become navigable graph objects without losing identity."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md storage/rendering fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Entities land in futon1a and render in WebArxana."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Recorded route interpreted through HDM.", :theory {: