{:i2 "chapter0-aif-as-wiring-diagram.md is identified as the canonical exposition."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and canonical document.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A wiring representation with a verifiable canonical basis."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph" 18], :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :roles ["rationale" "dependency"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph\" 18]", :span {:start 1554, :end 1622}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :square-digest "4dae9c7f2d2859620aa3e0adab84a8438c56ecefda020dfbe6e6a2319e766c5c"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern legibility requirement applied to the visual idiom.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether its diagrams reveal real mission objects, roles, transitions, and consequences in the shared stack."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The stack becomes inhabitable when its actual typed relationships are visibly represented."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Visual-idiom fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The canonical exposition supplies an autonomous War Machine visual idiom."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and exposition role.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A visual language that renders autonomous control as part of the actual stack world."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph" 19], :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :roles ["action" "goal"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph\" 19]", :span {:start 1623, :end 1651}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :square-digest "b2c85f5a86843b2abf8e3560bdbe39745ca13f08edd7d14f0b656b2e8c8839c0"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern world-legibility rule applied to per-mission emission.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether every selected mission receives a diagram of its real nodes, typed relationships, actions, and effects."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph IF/THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Agents need legible views of the shared mutable world they already inhabit."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Per-mission emission fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The War Machine should emit a visual representation for every mission."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and proposed emission.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A per-mission view through which operators can inspect and navigate autonomous behavior."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 20], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 20]", :span {:start 1652, :end 1718}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "67a317d4d6195bb3ab145d7349dbe0e06b49998d036d5de4e180a158d136e6cb"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Activation pattern applied to the existing capture.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether it reuses the captured mission data as a provenance-linked graph source rather than reconstructing it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Durable stored material should be activated in a coherent graph with provenance retained."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Mission-capture fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "futon2-aif-ants.edn is an existing durable capture of the AIF ants mission."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and data artifact.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Existing AIF mission data activated as a connected, source-traceable graph object."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 21], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 21]", :span {:start 1719, :end 1742}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "daf894cdce8cbfcf02475e2bc98b57b73ad769d2d6ff5e91f023352e6de023d6"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Pattern provenance rule applied to the captured data.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether the mission data participates in reasoning and visualization while retaining its original artifact link."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Stored records become useful across boundaries when graph activation preserves their identity."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Mission-data fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The captured artifact contains AIF-ants mission data."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and captured content.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Reusable AIF-ants mission evidence in the active stack graph."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 22], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 22]", :span {:start 1743, :end 1813}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :square-digest "3c1a365b2828da39cf5849db7a1f1a440d9816142427a4b552ff3d10516be3c7"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the trace precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by checking the proposed trace representation against the exact cited checkpoint."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A precedent claim needs a precise artifact or checkpoint anchor."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Checkpoint reference fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Checkpoint 6 of M-stack-stereolithography is cited as the piano-roll precedent."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and checkpoint reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A trace design with an independently inspectable precedent."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["war-machine/state-capture" 23], :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :roles ["action" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"war-machine/state-capture\" 23]", :span {:start 1814, :end 1872}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :square-digest "ec923c242de9faf0f7d3038371d7f2d38eb3f98d6216dfb059846bb1ba0361ab"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture checks applied to the piano roll.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether the trace exposes selections, time spent, and the outside obligation associated with each activity."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "War Machine activity needs observable checks showing what obligations it served."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Trace-projection fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The piano roll projects the head's post-hoc trace."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and trace role.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A post-hoc trace that reveals whether autonomous work served external or self-maintaining ends."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number" 24], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :roles ["context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number\" 24]", :span {:start 1873, :end 1893}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :square-digest "a7bd7335369c6b723333003f086958261635053d032bc4fc606a098143584ffb"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Measurement warrant applied to the trace axes.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether every plotted observation retains its substrate identity, timestamp, transformation rule, and exclusions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Recorded measurements must retain inputs, rules, and assumptions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Projection-axes fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The piano-roll trace is projected over substrate and time."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and projection axes.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A recomputable substrate-by-time trace whose plotted values remain contestable."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 25], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 25]", :span {:start 1894, :end 1962}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :square-digest "28336a7830540aceb91f2a11ccfb858f844bce893b483f9da61273c1727c997b"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to script and outputs.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by running the named renderer and inspecting the cited output forms against the claimed trace behavior."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Prototype claims need concrete implementation and output anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Prototype implementation fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "piano_roll.py and prototype PDF/PNG paths are cited as the renderer and outputs."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and artifact references.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A trace prototype whose production path and rendered evidence are inspectable."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["war-machine/state-capture" 26], :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :roles ["action" "context"]