0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined evidence pattern and runtime source references.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A recommendation grounded in inspectable runtime violation evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number" 10], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :roles ["dependency" "action"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-recommendation-bindings/M-recommendation-bindings/policy-7e8a0806fea29fa47914/[\"measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number\" 10]", :span {:start 1031, :end 1137}, :source-text-digest "e8678feb63133e7a13d5d3ed7a2722c430f8ff80f2355b6f98a4d09dd01fe941", :analysis-digest "54558739922fa7db94f035fc7573d430033fbee7e87acce089da6b5f4ed38441", :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :square-digest "a23b762c7ee3c80ad0feb533d66e3bc37e723c8d3e0b8b765750a89f0d10aac2"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Pattern warrant requirement applied to the proof-debt measurement.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whether proof-debt-sensitive recommendations retain the counter rule, boundary inputs, and relevant exclusions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A computed metric must carry its rule, inputs, and assumptions so a skeptical reader can recompute it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "M-recommendation-bindings proof-debt counter fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "devmap_readiness.py and boundary.edn produce an active per-prototype proof-debt count."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined measurement pattern and proof-debt counter reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A next-move recommendation whose proof-debt value is reproducible from its cited computation and data."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number" 11], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :roles ["dependency" "rationale" "action"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-recommendation-bindings/M-recommendation-bindings/policy-7e8a0806fea29fa47914/[\"measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number\" 11]", :span {:start 1138, :end 1271}, :source-text-digest "e8678feb63133e7a13d5d3ed7a2722c430f8ff80f2355b6f98a4d09dd01fe941", :analysis-digest "54558739922fa7db94f035fc7573d430033fbee7e87acce089da6b5f4ed38441", :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :square-digest "ab0b86ae8db96f32e2249a4fe21b627fc44c16b30ab6d053285cf378d590e0f6"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Pattern warrant discipline applied to the cited posterior construction.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whether its posterior-based policy preserves the prior, live evidence, join rule, and assumptions used to rank the complete set of moves."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a795