emain tied to grounded obligations."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md reference to M-mission-control.md.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Mission Control supplies the observational dependency."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Cross-reference constrained by external-obligation checks.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Use Mission Control as grounded input, not self-maintenance evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["war-machine/state-capture" 6], :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :roles ["context" "condition"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"war-machine/state-capture\" 6]", :span {:start 445, :end 489}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :square-digest "b2d629045086b97f206ff48d92debabb1835e22edb7fdcc251e51cef7b3ba4a4"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture rule and recorded portfolio scope.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The active portfolio grounds the geometry’s state."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Infrastructure should expose the outside work it supports."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md observation-scope fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Mission Control observes about 25 active missions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "~25-mission scope interpreted through state-capture.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Use active missions as the grounding population for geometry."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 7], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 7]", :span {:start 518, :end 542}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :square-digest "83fb3455d39614446631302a915da297a8ce565a356a09b7882f54c2133f01ad"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule and cited mission path.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The named mission and source tree anchor the inference claim."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Inference claims need inspectable anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md reference to M-portfolio-inference.md.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-portfolio-inference owns the inference layer."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Cross-reference under the pattern’s verification rule.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Verify portfolio-inference claims through its mission and code."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 8], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["context" "dependency"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 8]", :span {:start 584, :end 619}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :square-digest "2b977f26ca8bec5704d0c3e96e335ff7ba555ad7e05c03645f2ec4d218a8b7ec"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule plus M-portfolio-inference references.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The layer is checkable through adjacent mission and code references."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg IF/THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Architectural descriptions require verification paths."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md policy-layer fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "A generative-model and EFE layer is claimed above Mission Control."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Policy-layer fragment and preceding paths.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Anchor the EFE-layer claim to those concrete artifacts."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector" 9], :pattern "features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector\" 9]", :span {:start 670, :end 709}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "43bcf868e30e714fd129050aef2829e05ceb04cf40acce31d8644d864a3e779f", :square-digest "79c1f888c01c5c2d6db5d829d800067990b775c4834ee3393de211022c720bf9"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector", :objects {:G {:text "    WR-16 rules that an operationalised loop the operator actually runs is a\n    first-class observation channel, and the mark vocabulary is that loop: Joe\n    already types his own turns, in a vocabulary he partly named. What the\n    apparatus does with them today is measure how long it has been since he\n    appeared. The per-class credit collapse to 0.009 is what a missing variable\n    looks like from inside the model -- \"he considered this and declined\" and\n    \"he was elsewhere\" arrive at the estimator as the same event, so the\n    estimator learns that the operator is noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector.flexiarg", :sha256 "43bcf868e30e714fd129050aef2829e05ceb04cf40acce31d8644d864a3e779f"}, :situation-source "Feature’s observation-channel steps and hinge-log reference.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "A durable hinge log can carry operator acts into inference."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Operator turns are captured, typed, and text-searchable.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector.flexiarg", :sha256 "43bcf868e30e714fd129050aef2829e05ceb04cf40acce31d8644d864a3e779f"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Captured turns matter only when inference reads them."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The observation vector cannot see them, and the one place the apparatus\n    does claim to represent Joe is unwired.\n\n    `operator-lane/nag?` is a conjunction of four terms and the fourth is\n    `:acknowledged?`. Nothing sets it. `operator-lane-adapter` assembles nine\n    descriptive keys onto every item and that is not among them;\n    `operator-bulletin/newly-acknowledged` computes the acknowledged set as a\n    pure function and has no caller outside its own test, its docstring\n    deferring persistence to \"the forward-model adapter\" that does not do it;\n    the one path that bypasses the classifier with a pre-set lane reads\n    `data/wm/needs-you.edn`, which is `[]`. So nag 0 of 111 on the live\n    bulletin is not a threshold that wants tuning. The gate cannot open,\n    because the term that would open it has no producer -- and that term is\n    definitionally an operator turn: it means Joe LOOKED.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector.flexiarg", :sha256 "43bcf868e30e714fd129050aef2829e05ceb04cf40acce31d8644d864a3e779f"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md reference to M-trip-journal.md.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-trip-journal supplies a hinge-log apparatus."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Three steps, and only the third one closes the ring. Keep them separately\n    reviewable, because the first is cheap and reads like progress.\n\n    0. Wire acknowledgement. Persist `newly-acknowledged` at bulletin pull and\n       feed `:acknowledged?` back through the adapter. This makes nag reachable\n       and is worth doing -- but it is a repair to a dangling seam, NOT this\n       feature. Report it as such. (See FAILURE-MODES: it is separately\n       sufficient to satisfy the promotion test as first drafted, which is a\n       defect in that test rather than a licence to claim the ring.)\n    1. Emit an operator-turn observation. One channel appended to\n       `channel-keys`, normalised to [0,1] like its neighbours, whose value is\n       a function of the marks on turns addressed to the item -- the obvious\n       first cut being recent-correction-or-approval pressure, so that ✘ and ✓\n       are distinguishable and neither is confused with silence. State its\n       provenance the way `:selection-source` distinguishes an operator pick\n       from the selector's -- and prefer inbox-zero's three-class basis ranking\n       (:direct / :corroborated / :weak) to inventing a second vocabulary for\n       the same distinction.\n       The cheapest honest version reuses the followup queue rather than the\n       mark corpus: an :acked followup IS an operator turn -- durable,\n       exact-seat, already timestamped. Building the channel on acknowledgement\n       first gets a real operator act into the vector on rails that exist; the\n       mark corpus is the richer second source, not a prerequisite.\n    2. Show it is read. Run one window of >= 111 classifications with the\n       channel live, and the same window with it held at a constant, and record\n       both inference results.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/features/operator-turns-enter-the-observation-vector.flexiarg", :sha256 "43bcf868e30e714fd129050aef2829e05ceb04cf40acce31d8644d864a3e779f"}, :situation-source "Mission dependency plus emit-and-read requirements.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Feed hinge-log records into geometry and prove they are read."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph" 10], :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph\" 10]", :span {:start 715, :end 747}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :square-digest "d1ead7523340b413947b24d007ad143dbf938a76f01ff1e3ebe794ecfcb391a3"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "HDM provenance rule and shared substrate.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "One ingestion boundary activates records without erasing origins."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Stored records become active graph objects with provenance."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md shared-substrate fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Trip Journal and Stack Geometry share futon1a ingestion."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Shared ingestion dependency interpreted through HDM.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Activate trip-journal records through futon1a with provenance intact."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["problems/operator-turns-become-inference-observations" 12], :pattern "problems/operator-turns-become-inference-observations", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e1