iscipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Pattern warrant requirement applied to the proof-debt measurement.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a cascade by whether proof-debt-sensitive recommendations retain the counter rule, boundary inputs, and relevant exclusions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A computed metric must carry its rule, inputs, and assumptions so a skeptical reader can recompute it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "M-recommendation-bindings proof-debt counter fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "devmap_readiness.py and boundary.edn produce an active per-prototype proof-debt count."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n     